From 7510da2498592d8ad8960c6174a6ee2ba296c10a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 21:59:25 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] feat(deepseek-v4.1): batch-invariant GEMV backend behind an
 opt-in variable

The BF16-output V4.1 projections (index head weights, the index key and the
ratio-1 compressor) take the torch backend at capacities from 10 rows, and
cuBLAS picks its kernel by row count, so a row rounds differently with
different neighbours. On the traced prose target the ratio-1 compressor at
layer 20 was where its solo prefill and mixed batches first diverged.

With VLLM_DS41_BATCH_INVARIANT=1, capacities below 256 rows whose default is
the torch backend are planned on the SIMT GEMV instead, as the FP32-output
projections already are. Unset, the production setting, nothing changes.
